From a2790471682461512f337d862f392e08dc5ab979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 06:19:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: message timestamps (UTC parsing bug) + correct bubble
 sides and staff attribution
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Timestamps: shared new lib/timeUtils.ts utility that safely normalizes
backend timestamps (which have no timezone marker, causing JS to
misread them as local time — off by exactly Nigeria's UTC+1 offset,
which is why everything showed roughly '1h ago'). Applied consistently
across both messaging pages, the floating message widget, and all 5
role-based notification pages.

Messaging bubbles + attribution: updated dealer and staff messages pages
to match the backend's new sender-resolution fix — staff view now
compares against the conversation's dealerUserId (not their own personal
id) when in synced 'dealer' mode, so their own sent messages correctly
show on their own side instead of clumping with the other party. Both
dealer and staff views now show a small attribution label (their name,
'You', or the dealer's name) under each message so it's clear who on
the team actually sent it, without that identity ever leaking to the
external party.
